          %h3#in_the_dual_numbers In the dual numbers
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+number"} dual number
            real algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔻
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D} \coloneqq \mathbb{R}[\epsilon]/\epsilon^2
            has a notion of sine and cosine function, which are the solutions to the system of functional equations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi sin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi cos
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi ϵ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sin(x + \epsilon) = \sin(x) + \cos(x) \epsilon
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cos
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi cos
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi sin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi ϵ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cos(x + \epsilon) = \cos(x) - \sin(x) \epsilon
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sin
